flowchart LR
    USER[Support users: L1 / L2 / L3 / Admin] --> UI[React + Vite single-page application]
    UI -->|Bearer token, JSON| API[FastAPI REST API]

    subgraph AUTHZ[API and Access Control]
        API --> AUTH[Authentication and role authorization]
        API --> INCIDENT[Search, triage, resolve, ticket workflow]
        API --> FEEDBACK[Feedback, profiles, notifications]
        API --> ADMIN[Users, analytics, evaluation, provider settings]
    end

    subgraph PIPELINE[Incident Intelligence Pipeline]
        GUARD[Input guardrails and PII filtering] --> TRIAGE[Classification, priority, SLA, routing]
        TRIAGE --> RETRIEVE[Hybrid retrieval and metadata filters]
        RETRIEVE --> RCA[Root cause analysis]
        RCA --> ANSWER[Grounded resolution assistance]
        ANSWER --> SAFE[Safety and grounding validation]
        SAFE --> TICKET[L1 to L2 to L3 ticket handoff]
    end
    INCIDENT --> GUARD
    TICKET --> API

    subgraph INDEX[Local Incident Knowledge Base]
        CSV[data/incidents.csv] --> PREP[Normalize, clean, deduplicate, searchable text]
        PREP --> CORPUS[Incident descriptions and resolutions]
        CORPUS --> WORD[Word n-gram TF-IDF]
        CORPUS --> CHAR[Character n-gram TF-IDF]
        CORPUS --> SEM[Local SVD semantic vectors]
        CORPUS --> TOKENS[Keyword / token overlap]
        WORD --> RANK[Weighted ranking and local reranking]
        CHAR --> RANK
        SEM --> RANK
        TOKENS --> RANK
    end
    RANK --> RETRIEVE

    subgraph PROVIDERS[Optional LLM Providers and Offline Fallback]
        ANSWER --> KEYS[OpenRouter / Google Gemini / OpenAI]
        KEYS -->|Enabled and configured| LLM[Grounded provider answer]
        KEYS -->|Disabled, missing key, or unavailable| FALLBACK[Local evidence and deterministic fallback]
        LLM --> SAFE
        FALLBACK --> SAFE
    end

    subgraph DB[SQLite Persistence]
        USERS[(Users and role profiles)]
        TICKETS[(Tickets and handoff event history)]
        OTHER[(Feedback, incidents, settings, notifications, audit, search history)]
    end
    AUTH <--> USERS
    INCIDENT <--> TICKETS
    INCIDENT <--> OTHER
    FEEDBACK <--> OTHER
    ADMIN <--> OTHER
    PREP -->|Admin-created incidents| OTHER

    subgraph EVAL[Evaluation]
        CASES[Representative incident queries] --> METRICS[Precision@1, Hit Rate@3/5, MRR, MAP, latency]
        METRICS --> REPORT[evaluation_results.json and Admin Evaluation Studio]
    end
    RETRIEVE --> CASES
